| <!DOCTYPE html>
| <html>
|   <head>
|     "
"
|     <meta>
|       charset="utf-8"
|     "
"
|     <title>
|       "browser: floats"
|     "
"
|     <style>
|       "
body { margin: 16px; font-family: sans-serif; background: #ffffff; color: #1f2a37; }
.left { float: left; width: 120px; height: 90px; margin: 0 12px 8px 0; background: #6aa0e8; }
.right { float: right; width: 150px; height: 60px; margin: 0 0 8px 12px; background: #e89c6a; }
.note { float: right; padding: 6px 10px; background: #f3e3a2; }
.clear { clear: both; background: #dfe8d0; padding: 4px; }
.box { background: #f0f0f0; padding: 8px; margin: 8px 0; }
.tile { float: left; width: 100px; height: 40px; margin: 4px; background: #9fd5b4; }
h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }
p { margin: 0 0 10px 0; }
"
|     "
"
|   "
"
|   <body>
|     "
"
|     <h1>
|       "Floats"
|     "
"
|     <div>
|       class="left"
|     "
"
|     <div>
|       class="right"
|     "
"
|     <p>
|       "The text of this paragraph flows around a float on the left and a float on the right. Each line is as wide as the
floats beside it leave, so the lines next to the floats are shorter than the lines under them. Once the text goes past
the bottom of a float, the line takes the width back on that side and runs to the edge of the page again."
|     "
"
|     <p>
|       "A second paragraph continues beside the taller float: its lines start after the float on the left until the float
ends, then they start at the left edge."
|     "
"
|     <div>
|       class="clear"
|       "This block clears both floats: it starts below the lower of the two."
|     "
"
|     <div>
|       class="box"
|       <span>
|         class="note"
|         "a float in the text"
|       "A float inside a line of text goes to the right side of this
box, at the top of its content, and the words of the line wrap around it."
|     "
"
|     <div>
|       class="box"
|       "
"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       "
"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       <div>
|         class="tile"
|       "
"
|       <div>
|         class="clear"
|         "After the tiles, which wrap onto a second row when the first is full."
|       "
"
|     "


"
